<title>JAPAN: IHI raises overseas sales target 30 pct.</title>
<headline>IHI raises overseas sales target 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ishikawajima-Harima Heavy Industries Co Ltd (IHI) said on Monday it aims to boost the value of its overseas contracts for industrial plants in 1997/98 to between 120 billion and 130 billion yen, up 30 percent from the previous business year.</p>
<p>It had initially aimed to boost orders for constructing industrial plants overseas to that figure in 2000/2001. But it decided to target the figure in the current business year due to robust demand from Asia, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The weaker yen has helped the company's competitiveness against European and U.S. firms, he said.</p>
</text>
